implementationPlan.description:
Test first. Create packages/moe-daemon/src/server/WebSocketServer.unblockOwner.test.ts with your own editor (Write on Claude, apply_patch on codex exec), never a shell copy. Start from the architect's prototype at /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-21702095/WebSocketServer.unblockOwner.test.ts (102 lines). It ports the filing repro /mnt/d/moe-scratch/hunt-a133-ws/zzWsUnblockCorpse.test.ts and adds one control.

Setup: a real MoeWebSocketServer on an ephemeral 127.0.0.1 port, the WebSocketServer.transitions.test.ts pattern. Five BLOCKED rows (blockedFromStatus WORKING, blockedResourceId gpu-box) are assigned to:
- worker-gone: no record;
- worker-idle: IDLE with currentTaskId null, the blocked-timeout corpse shape;
- worker-dead: DEAD, pointing at the row;
- worker-held: BLOCKED, pointing at the row (the genuine hold);
- worker-idle-held: IDLE but still pointing at the row. parkedHoldOwner keeps this one too (mem:gotcha-resource-parked-unblock-regression).

Each row is moved with UPDATE_TASK {status: 'WORKING'}. The test asserts the exact table {reply, status, assignedWorkerId, claimable (state.isTaskClaimable), blockedFromStatus}:
- the first three: assignedWorkerId null, claimable true;
- the last two keep their assignee, claimable false;
- all five: TASK_UPDATED, WORKING, blockedFromStatus null.

Architect RED proof at 0f56d3a7: 1 failed, with ghost/corpse/dead received as worker-gone/worker-idle/worker-dead and corpse claimable false.

Error handling in the test: the frame wait gives up after about 5 s with 'no frame' instead of hanging. afterEach closes the sockets, the server, the HTTP listener and the temp dir.

Verification. Run it once, before moe.complete_task; its fresh output is the completion evidence. From the task worktree root, run the executionContract checkRef exactly as written. The same text (998 bytes) is at /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-21702095/checkref-gate.txt.
- What it does:
  - overlays the two owned code files onto a whole-tree `git archive HEAD` snapshot (mem:gotcha-harness-snapshot-needs-full-archive, mem:gotcha-daemon-linux-snapshot-gate);
  - checks structurally that the exit arm calls `parkedHoldOwner(this.state, existing)`, that the old `assignedWorkerId: existing.assignedWorkerId }` restore is gone, and that the entry arm's `assignedWorkerId: existing.assignedWorkerId,` is still there;
  - under env -i with nvm Node v24.21.0 and NO_COLOR=1, runs `npm ci` and vitest on the new file, WebSocketServer.transitions.test.ts and the setTaskStatus suites.
- Expected: exit 0, 'Test Files  5 passed (5)', and a last line of 'unblockOwner ok (/tmp/m2170.XXXX)'.
- Architect dry runs, from a --shared clone at 0f56d3a7 with this plan's prototype uncommitted:
  - this command: exit 0, 5 files and 47 tests in about 5 s;
  - the same command against the unfixed handler stops with 'exit arm (...)' and exit 1;
  - the full daemon suite with the prototype: 279 files, 7428 passed, 24 skipped.
- Then rm -rf the printed literal /tmp/m2170.XXXX path.
- Never run npm in the shared checkout, and never pattern-kill a process.
- Error handling: on a non-zero exit, read the printed path and the log tail first, then fix the earlier steps' files.
